{"author":{"id":"a3a282966ced55effb4560271fcd98e13241af24ea76b00ec76a0f18154bc8ee"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1790190808,"nonce":"T/uXiod3wpsjl33G5+Z67r9b9ac=","message":"Decision (Luis, 2026-09-23): the Starlark host API mirrors the command line one to one. Every `git work issue|schema|flow \u003cverb\u003e` is a function of the same name under a module of the same name, with the same arguments, returning what the command prints as JSON. Nothing is reachable from a script that the shell cannot reach, and vice versa; the only script-only names are `me()` and the `render.*` constructors. Recorded in doc/design/config-entity.md E9.","files":null}]}